## 2.1 Generate my work plan

ServiceNow's current Platform Generate my work plan agentic workflow creates personalized work plans for assigned work.

It identifies assigned work, predicts effort using historical records, and generates an actionable work plan.

The documented prioritization inputs include:

- user sentiment;
- short description;
- priority;
- description;
- due date;
- escalation;
- state;
- updated time;
- impact;
- SLA.

The workflow provides reasoning for its decisions.

ServiceNow also documents a **Prioritize work AI Agent**, which dynamically orders tasks using factors such as urgency, priority, SLAs, sentiment, and impact.

Source:

https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/generate-work-plan.html

**Classification: DIRECT EVIDENCE**

# 7. Exception Queue Visibility

ServiceNow's Purchase Order Management workspace provides:

- top exceptions;
- priority sorting;
- elapsed time;
- open exceptions by priority;
- incoming exception tasks;
- new activity;
- in-progress exceptions;
- task workload.

Source:

https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/source-to-pay-operations/source-to-pay-workspace/purch-order-mgmt-tab-s2pws.html

This provides an operational mechanism for humans to see and act on prioritized exception queues.

**Classification: DIRECT EVIDENCE**

# 8. Jefferies Revisited

The Jefferies customer evidence is particularly important because it describes the exact legacy problem that motivated OPP-002.

The legacy team manually:

- filtered exceptions;
- classified exceptions;
- prioritized exceptions;
- sorted emails;
- assigned work;
- correlated communications.

After implementing ServiceNow, managers could:

- assess risk;
- prioritize;
- categorize;
- assign exceptions;
- analyze exceptions by location or client;
- focus on high-priority problems.

Source:

https://www.servicenow.com/customers/jefferies.html

The customer explicitly states that ServiceNow provides easy prioritization and faster resolution.

Source:

https://www.servicenow.com/content/dam/servicenow-assets/public/en-us/doc-type/resource-center/case-study/cs-jefferies.pdf

**Classification: VERIFIED EXTERNAL EVIDENCE**

